u}^{i}+(1-\alpha_{t}){ m{1}}_{K} and ℓ i \ell_{i} denotes the non-zero index of 𝒛 t i { m{z}}_{t}^{i} . Recent UDM formulations. Among several recent UDM formulations, we focus on two representative frameworks: Diffusion Duality ( Sahoo et al., 2025 ) and the leave-one-out formulation of Gourevitch et al. (2026) . Diffusion Duality retains the same uniform forward process and UDM NELBO, but represents the uniform-state marginal through the arg ​ max \argmax of a Gaussian corruption and uses a curriculum from continuous relaxations to discrete inputs. In contrast, Gourevitch et al. (2026) show that the neural predictor in the UDM bridge has the leave-one-out (LOO) posterior as its population optimum: each clean token is predicted from the corrupted context excluding the observation at that same position, see Eq. ( 4 ). They further derive an analytic local-token correction that converts the LOO predictor into the full denoising posterior, allowing the underlying predictor to be trained with a simple cross-entropy loss. We refer to this CE-trained formulation as LOO+CE .

